(1673128, 224008, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2<br/>Contrast/Color: 1/2<br/>Composition: 2/2<br/>Photo Quality: 1/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 1/2</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2Contrast/Color: 1/2Composition: 2/2Photo Quality: 1/2My Subjective Affinity: 1/2', '2005-09-04 16:02:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1673130, 224236, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2<br/>Color/Contrast: 2/2<br/>Composition: 1/2<br/>Photo Quality: 1/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 2/2</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2Color/Contrast: 2/2Composition: 1/2Photo Quality: 1/2My Subjective Affinity: 2/2', '2005-09-04 16:02:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1673133, 224772, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 1/2<br/>Contrast/Color: 2/2<br/>Composition: 1/2<br/>Photo Quality: 1/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 1/2</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 1/2Contrast/Color: 2/2Composition: 1/2Photo Quality: 1/2My Subjective Affinity: 1/2', '2005-09-04 16:03:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1673134, 225016, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2<br/>Color/Contrast: 0/2<br/>Composition: 1/2<br/>Photo Quality: 1/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 1/2</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2Color/Contrast: 0/2Composition: 1/2Photo Quality: 1/2My Subjective Affinity: 1/2', '2005-09-04 16:04:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1673139, 222838, 22379, '<td valign="top">Those purple shoes are craz - how on earth do you walk in them?<br/>Attnetion to detail is important. This was  astatic shot, so there is no reason why this image should have been entered when you could go bakc and take one without the edge of the cardboard box showing.</td>', 'Those purple shoes are craz - how on earth do you walk in them?Attnetion to detail is important. This was  astatic shot, so there is no reason why this image should have been entered when you could go bakc and take one without the edge of the cardboard box showing.', '2005-09-04 16:05:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1673140, 224986, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 1/2<br/>Color/Contrast: 0/2<br/>Composition: 0/2<br/>Photo Quality: 0/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 0/2</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 1/2Color/Contrast: 0/2Composition: 0/2Photo Quality: 0/2My Subjective Affinity: 0/2', '2005-09-04 16:06:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1673142, 225058, 42837, '<td valign="top">I like the textures. should be cropped differently to improve the composition which could have more structure. And I end up roaming about the picture looking for something focused to rest my eyes on, but there''s none.</td>', 'I like the textures. should be cropped differently to improve the composition which could have more structure. And I end up roaming about the picture looking for something focused to rest my eyes on, but there''s none.', '2005-09-04 16:07:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1673148, 224473, 42837, '<td valign="top">Awkward crop, losing the left toe. Should be a portrait composition maybe, and the pristine wood pannelling doesn''t suit the title at all. It also seems that the floor is more sharpply focused than the boots.</td>', 'Awkward crop, losing the left toe. Should be a portrait composition maybe, and the pristine wood pannelling doesn''t suit the title at all. It also seems that the floor is more sharpply focused than the boots.', '2005-09-04 16:09:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1673160, 223360, 25655, '<td valign="top">I was really surprised to see how many shots there are, trying to get this angle of the shoe.<br/>The most of them, however, tried to focus on teh shoe, instead of the lace hole, which is actually the interesting thing, since this is where the shape changes.<br/>This is just a great picture! interesting, hard to tell if it''s a real one or a statue, and I am a long time sucker for shallow DOF.<br/>Say, is that blur should really be there? sorry... couldn''t resist.<br/>Very nice take on this oh-so-boring challenge! 8</td>', 'I was really surprised to see how many shots there are, trying to get this angle of the shoe.The most of them, however, tried to focus on teh shoe, instead of the lace hole, which is actually the interesting thing, since this is where the shape changes.This is just a great picture! interesting, hard to tell if it''s a real one or a statue, and I am a long time sucker for shallow DOF.Say, is that blur should really be there? sorry... couldn''t resist.Very nice take on this oh-so-boring challenge! 8', '2005-09-04 16:23:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1673162, 223983, 25655, '<td valign="top">Should have titled "Try walking in my shoes".<br/>Wonderful idea. A little bit lacks in contrast IMO, but other then that a real nice idea. 8</td>', 'Should have titled "Try walking in my shoes".Wonderful idea. A little bit lacks in contrast IMO, but other then that a real nice idea. 8', '2005-09-04 16:25:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1673163, 224868, 25655, '<td valign="top">what a lovely idea! so sweet :-)<br/>I wish the grass under it was real though. Could have add so much more interest to the shot! 7</td>', 'what a lovely idea! so sweet :-)I wish the grass under it was real though. Could have add so much more interest to the shot! 7', '2005-09-04 16:26:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1673164, 223027, 22379, '<td valign="top">a bare foot kind of misses the purpose of the challenge. <br/>Since you did ask what you could have done differently on the boards her e is what i would have done. Destaurated the carpet - the different colour speckles are distracting.<br/>Either focused the camera on babies face, or if you really wanted it to be a feet photo used a shallowed DOF and focused completely on the feet. Right now the focus seems to be the bum. <br/>Gotten a little more above baby, more looking srtairght down so not to hieghtlight the paer shape the diaper makes the baby appeear to have (personally i would have used a nude baby but thats just me)<br/>I do like the placement of the baby in the frame - as far as DNMC photos go, this is definately in the top.</td>', 'a bare foot kind of misses the purpose of the challenge. Since you did ask what you could have done differently on the boards her e is what i would have done. Destaurated the carpet - the different colour speckles are distracting.Either focused the camera on babies face, or if you really wanted it to be a feet photo used a shallowed DOF and focused completely on the feet. Right now the focus seems to be the bum. Gotten a little more above baby, more looking srtairght down so not to hieghtlight the paer shape the diaper makes the baby appeear to have (personally i would have used a nude baby but thats just me)I do like the placement of the baby in the frame - as far as DNMC photos go, this is definately in the top.', '2005-09-04 16:27:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1673166, 223468, 22379, '<td valign="top">The lighting is too harsh on the right side. Don''t go for a "perfect white" background if it means losing quality in the sunject matter.</td>', 'The lighting is too harsh on the right side. Don''t go for a "perfect white" background if it means losing quality in the sunject matter.', '2005-09-04 16:28:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1673167, 223981, 25655, '<td valign="top">GREAT use of shallow DOF!! Works just wonderful here!!!<br/>I bet you''re being hummered though... people here wouldn''t recognize a good shot even if it fell on their heads... 10</td>', 'GREAT use of shallow DOF!! Works just wonderful here!!!I bet you''re being hummered though... people here wouldn''t recognize a good shot even if it fell on their heads... 10', '2005-09-04 16:28:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1673168, 223299, 31403, '<td valign="top">this is really beautiful, I would love to see whiter whites, but just full of emotion</td>', 'this is really beautiful, I would love to see whiter whites, but just full of emotion', '2005-09-04 16:28:49.000000', NULL, 1),
