(1673757, 222418, 40976, '<td valign="top">Interesting lighting ... How''d you do that?  My guess is long exposure and some kind of flashlight?  Nice unique concept.  :)</td>', 'Interesting lighting ... How''d you do that?  My guess is long exposure and some kind of flashlight?  Nice unique concept.  :)', '2005-09-04 22:05:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1673760, 224611, 40976, '<td valign="top">I can only imagine how difficult it was to get the dog to cooperate.  Nice job with the capture.</td>', 'I can only imagine how difficult it was to get the dog to cooperate.  Nice job with the capture.', '2005-09-04 22:06:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1673762, 224172, 40819, '<td valign="top">nice color consistency</td>', 'nice color consistency', '2005-09-04 22:08:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1673768, 222938, 42837, '<td valign="top">Good use of DOF. Although it looks a bit like the pose of the following shoe is kinda artifical just so it can be fully visible beside the front shoe. It would seem more natural if the perspective caused some of it to be obscured behind the front shoe. And I know this may seem like nitpicking (that''s what happens with a good idea that''s well executed) but maybe there should be some contact with the ground (even the heel of the shoe perhaps) to really carry through the effect of grip and friction.  9</td>', 'Good use of DOF. Although it looks a bit like the pose of the following shoe is kinda artifical just so it can be fully visible beside the front shoe. It would seem more natural if the perspective caused some of it to be obscured behind the front shoe. And I know this may seem like nitpicking (that''s what happens with a good idea that''s well executed) but maybe there should be some contact with the ground (even the heel of the shoe perhaps) to really carry through the effect of grip and friction.  9', '2005-09-04 22:10:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1673774, 223518, 40976, '<td valign="top">Nice job.  You''ll have to let us know how you got the upside down shoe in the lense like that.  :)</td>', 'Nice job.  You''ll have to let us know how you got the upside down shoe in the lense like that.  :)', '2005-09-04 22:11:40.000000', NULL, 1),
