(1681014, 222875, 39038, '<td valign="top">What the h#$@? this photo is my second highest scored entry. And I really did not expect it. I did this photo in only 30 minutes in total. I just thought to submit something. not really paying too much attention like I did on other entries. I guess it is really hard to explain what people likes...<br/> <br/>Anyway, I found majority of commentors were bothered by the little stone. lol. I am sorry for that. I will remove it next time. :D<br/> <br/>As for how to take this photo. It is rather easy. I have my boots ready, obviously. I put them on my white carpet in front of a white wall. Then put my camera on the floor too. then use the builtin meter to make white wall and carpet slight over exposed. In PS, I rotated it 26.8 degree (If I remembered correctly). Just regular post processing. I did played curve intensively though.<br/> <br/>Thanks again for your vote (high or low) and comments!</td>', 'What the h#$@? this photo is my second highest scored entry. And I really did not expect it. I did this photo in only 30 minutes in total. I just thought to submit something. not really paying too much attention like I did on other entries. I guess it is really hard to explain what people likes... Anyway, I found majority of commentors were bothered by the little stone. lol. I am sorry for that. I will remove it next time. :D As for how to take this photo. It is rather easy. I have my boots ready, obviously. I put them on my white carpet in front of a white wall. Then put my camera on the floor too. then use the builtin meter to make white wall and carpet slight over exposed. In PS, I rotated it 26.8 degree (If I remembered correctly). Just regular post processing. I did played curve intensively though. Thanks again for your vote (high or low) and comments!', '2005-09-07 01:22:59.000000', NULL, 0),
