(1681267, 224255, 12253, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!  Finally a bike shot in the winners circle.  I assume you did this similarly to the way I did mine for speed--by mounting the camera to the bike (I attached via my monopod to do it).  <br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=203276" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/357/thumb/203276.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/357/thumb/203276.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/357/thumb/203276.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>But you got such a great angle there, I''d love to see the setup.  <br/> <br/>Congratulations!</td>', 'Congratulations!  Finally a bike shot in the winners circle.  I assume you did this similarly to the way I did mine for speed--by mounting the camera to the bike (I attached via my monopod to do it).     But you got such a great angle there, I''d love to see the setup.   Congratulations!', '2005-09-07 02:15:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(1681311, 224976, 42402, '<td valign="top">After Challenge:<br/>Okay people, lets get one thing straight. That square-ish thing next to the shoes? Its NOT a bran muffin, brownie, muffin, or any type of food. Frankly I have no clue WHAT that is. (It was just on the table when I took this picture, and I thought, what the heck.) I know I kind of risked a lot using this picture, and I definitely know I went a little overboard with the wild colors. (I got all saturization happy) Apparently not the best picture I couldve taken, and not the best picture Ive editted (so far). Hopefully I''ll do better in the next competition. And I''ll be sure to remember not to have a confusing title or objects in my photo that look like random bits of bran muffins. <br/> <br/>(Thanks to those who pointed that out, I never would''ve noticed)</td>', 'After Challenge:Okay people, lets get one thing straight. That square-ish thing next to the shoes? Its NOT a bran muffin, brownie, muffin, or any type of food. Frankly I have no clue WHAT that is. (It was just on the table when I took this picture, and I thought, what the heck.) I know I kind of risked a lot using this picture, and I definitely know I went a little overboard with the wild colors. (I got all saturization happy) Apparently not the best picture I couldve taken, and not the best picture Ive editted (so far). Hopefully I''ll do better in the next competition. And I''ll be sure to remember not to have a confusing title or objects in my photo that look like random bits of bran muffins.  (Thanks to those who pointed that out, I never would''ve noticed)', '2005-09-07 02:25:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1681373, 223831, 15305, '<td valign="top">At last!!!  You deserved a ribbon since long time ago!!  Congratulations on your first blue.  I really admire your work!!</td>', 'At last!!!  You deserved a ribbon since long time ago!!  Congratulations on your first blue.  I really admire your work!!', '2005-09-07 02:44:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1681396, 224578, 40703, '<td valign="top">A little too much to handle. I DO like how the wine glass is under the heel of the one shoe, though I would have preferred more interaction between the pearls and the wine glasses. In the back I felt that the wine glass needed more wine. I can hardly see the glass otherwise.<br/> <br/>About the first comment: there''s a little too much implied in this photo. I don''t mean that in reference to the condom packages, but rather in general, though the packages do feel superfluous to this still life. Perhaps another candle to the right of the other heel and no flash at all would have made this photo more sensual and appealing than the stark, bright light. Rather than romantic it feels intrusive.<br/> <br/>So, that''s my critique. =)</td>', 'A little too much to handle. I DO like how the wine glass is under the heel of the one shoe, though I would have preferred more interaction between the pearls and the wine glasses. In the back I felt that the wine glass needed more wine. I can hardly see the glass otherwise. About the first comment: there''s a little too much implied in this photo. I don''t mean that in reference to the condom packages, but rather in general, though the packages do feel superfluous to this still life. Perhaps another candle to the right of the other heel and no flash at all would have made this photo more sensual and appealing than the stark, bright light. Rather than romantic it feels intrusive. So, that''s my critique. =)', '2005-09-07 02:52:12.000000', NULL, 0),
