(1681914, 223209, 9232, '<td valign="top">I love the colors in this shot and the composition.  Did your original shot have you off-center or did you crop it this way?  Creative setup!  Congratulations.</td>', 'I love the colors in this shot and the composition.  Did your original shot have you off-center or did you crop it this way?  Creative setup!  Congratulations.', '2005-09-07 08:59:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1681957, 224852, 35357, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the great shot, mesmeraj.  Even if you find it distasteful to be so in the box, it''s still a great shot, got a 10 from my general public vote.  You''re one of the best creative minds on DPC, IMO, and that''s saying a lot.  I don''t think 4th place is good enough for you, I think you should sell out until you get a Blue, which you''re certainly capable &amp; deserving of.  I love your imagination &amp; the way you capture it in pixels.  I''d sell my soul for a ribbon.  Bravo to you, you sell out! ;-)</td>', 'Congrats on the great shot, mesmeraj.  Even if you find it distasteful to be so in the box, it''s still a great shot, got a 10 from my general public vote.  You''re one of the best creative minds on DPC, IMO, and that''s saying a lot.  I don''t think 4th place is good enough for you, I think you should sell out until you get a Blue, which you''re certainly capable & deserving of.  I love your imagination & the way you capture it in pixels.  I''d sell my soul for a ribbon.  Bravo to you, you sell out! ;-)', '2005-09-07 09:14:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(1681963, 224852, 37961, '<td valign="top">WOAH!  4th place!! Amazing. Congrats!! What an achievement with so many entries!</td>', 'WOAH!  4th place!! Amazing. Congrats!! What an achievement with so many entries!', '2005-09-07 09:15:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1681999, 223831, 4482, '<td valign="top">Love it! Congrats!!</td>', 'Love it! Congrats!!', '2005-09-07 09:26:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682016, 224219, 30049, '<td valign="top">Thanks everybody for the comments and feedback.  I would like to address a couple of items that came up more than once.<br/> <br/>1) Color of the wood.  The wood is as it appeared.  I split a few pieces from the pile in the background, so it''s fresh split.  It started raining after I had everything setup so I packed up the camera until the rain ended (it was a light drizzle really).  The wood being wet, took on a darker more saturated tone.<br/> <br/>2) No lumberjack.  Well, the lumberjack is me - part time around the house anyway, therefore I couldn''t be in the boots and in the photo at the same time.  Actually, I never really thought about it since it was a shoe challenge.  Guess, I could have set the 10 second timer.  That would have been interesting!  ;^)<br/> <br/>As for the rest of the wood pile, it''s going to wait for splitting.  It''s not up in rotation until next summer...besides, I might need it for a prop again.  He-he.</td>', 'Thanks everybody for the comments and feedback.  I would like to address a couple of items that came up more than once. 1) Color of the wood.  The wood is as it appeared.  I split a few pieces from the pile in the background, so it''s fresh split.  It started raining after I had everything setup so I packed up the camera until the rain ended (it was a light drizzle really).  The wood being wet, took on a darker more saturated tone. 2) No lumberjack.  Well, the lumberjack is me - part time around the house anyway, therefore I couldn''t be in the boots and in the photo at the same time.  Actually, I never really thought about it since it was a shoe challenge.  Guess, I could have set the 10 second timer.  That would have been interesting!  ;^) As for the rest of the wood pile, it''s going to wait for splitting.  It''s not up in rotation until next summer...besides, I might need it for a prop again.  He-he.', '2005-09-07 09:34:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682041, 223303, 10909, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by stam:</b></div><hr/><i> The lighting is a bit off and a lot have done black and white but I like the originality. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The critique is welcomed :) From your comments, guys and ladies, I see that my idea of lighting was wrong...</td>', 'Originally posted by stam: The lighting is a bit off and a lot have done black and white but I like the originality.   The critique is welcomed :) From your comments, guys and ladies, I see that my idea of lighting was wrong...', '2005-09-07 09:47:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682043, 223831, 37005, '<td valign="top">With 461 entries I hadn''t seen this one but I wish I would''ve.  Great job.  Great concept.<br/> <br/>ANd thanks for the earworm.  Congrats!!</td>', 'With 461 entries I hadn''t seen this one but I wish I would''ve.  Great job.  Great concept. ANd thanks for the earworm.  Congrats!!', '2005-09-07 09:48:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682048, 224008, 37005, '<td valign="top">I like this shot.  A LOT.  Great composition.  Terrific concept.  Well deserved ribbon!!</td>', 'I like this shot.  A LOT.  Great composition.  Terrific concept.  Well deserved ribbon!!', '2005-09-07 09:50:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682058, 223303, 10909, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mesmeraj:</b></div><hr/><i> i do not understand your title. <br/>The streak of sunlight is blowing out your subject matter and does not compliment to the image in the least. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The title meant that mushroom mornings for these old boots are over... :) But since i have to explain this - maybe the title wasn''t good enough :(<br/> <br/>By this bright sun rays I wanted to emphasize the title: the sun is already up, but boots are still here: they "won''t go" for mushrooms :)</td>', 'Originally posted by mesmeraj: i do not understand your title. The streak of sunlight is blowing out your subject matter and does not compliment to the image in the least.   The title meant that mushroom mornings for these old boots are over... :) But since i have to explain this - maybe the title wasn''t good enough :( By this bright sun rays I wanted to emphasize the title: the sun is already up, but boots are still here: they "won''t go" for mushrooms :)', '2005-09-07 09:54:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682061, 223303, 10909, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by terje:</b></div><hr/><i> Interesting shot, like the angle.  Good luck ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks! I will try to do better next time.</td>', 'Originally posted by terje: Interesting shot, like the angle.  Good luck ;-)   Thanks! I will try to do better next time.', '2005-09-07 09:54:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682064, 223303, 10909, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pixieland:</b></div><hr/><i> I am sure it''s me, I just don''t see it. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Huh? :)</td>', 'Originally posted by pixieland: I am sure it''s me, I just don''t see it.   Huh? :)', '2005-09-07 09:55:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682068, 223303, 10909, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by racb:</b></div><hr/><i> interesting shot, all most like a still life. I wish the sunlight hadn''t been quite so intense- I found it pretty distracting. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ok, I see that my idea with sun rays failed :(<br/>Thanks for opinion.</td>', 'Originally posted by racb: interesting shot, all most like a still life. I wish the sunlight hadn''t been quite so intense- I found it pretty distracting.   Ok, I see that my idea with sun rays failed :(Thanks for opinion.', '2005-09-07 09:56:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682070, 223303, 10909, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by KiwiPix:</b></div><hr/><i> Because of the strong direct sunlight, you need to either filter it or add some fill light into the dark areas. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I guess you''re right - I will use some fill lights in future shots if the shot lacks the light...<br/> <br/>Thanks.</td>', 'Originally posted by KiwiPix: Because of the strong direct sunlight, you need to either filter it or add some fill light into the dark areas.   I guess you''re right - I will use some fill lights in future shots if the shot lacks the light... Thanks.', '2005-09-07 09:58:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682071, 224255, 32118, '<td valign="top">PAra quem tira fotos de esportes como eu , achei essa foto sensacional, parabéns !!!!!!</td>', 'PAra quem tira fotos de esportes como eu , achei essa foto sensacional, parabéns !!!!!!', '2005-09-07 09:58:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682094, 224008, 42792, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!  I didn''t vote but if I had this would have come out top for the emotion it evokes: a nice feel of child-like playfulness, a simple enjoyment of togetherness and freedom, the differences between the bare feet and shoe reflecting the idea of each to his or her own.  I don''t know if I''m making sense but anyway, well done.</td>', 'Congratulations!  I didn''t vote but if I had this would have come out top for the emotion it evokes: a nice feel of child-like playfulness, a simple enjoyment of togetherness and freedom, the differences between the bare feet and shoe reflecting the idea of each to his or her own.  I don''t know if I''m making sense but anyway, well done.', '2005-09-07 10:04:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682096, 224008, 22872, '<td valign="top">Love this shot!  Somehow I didn''t see it when I voted....weird...but congratulations!!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Love this shot!  Somehow I didn''t see it when I voted....weird...but congratulations!! ', '2005-09-07 10:05:51.000000', NULL, 0),
