(1682565, 223209, 13026, '<td valign="top">Congrats on 18th Anna!!<br/>You''re just too awesome.</td>', 'Congrats on 18th Anna!!You''re just too awesome.', '2005-09-07 12:27:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682621, 222942, 34906, '<td valign="top">BIG AL,<br/>Sometimes I am dumfounded and dismayed when I read some of the comments posted during voting.  One here is regretable and unforgivable and you certainly know which one that is.  I have been in this community for three months and there were a few times when I could have thrown in the towel after the cavalier, almost abusive tones of some comments.  Fortunately I have a relatively thick skin (comes from 65 years of taking life''s lumps.)  I persevered through my early attempts which were rated as low 4''s, even a 3+.  I have learned from the criticisms of mature, well-meaning members, and now have a few 6+''s under my belt.  I love the idea you went after in this challenge and I would hope that you would browse the forums so that you can match up the comments with the people who made them.  This would allow you to "consider the source."<br/>Basically, I hope you don''t get discouraged.  You obviously have a great sense of humor and creativity.  Go for it!<br/>Larry</td>', 'BIG AL,Sometimes I am dumfounded and dismayed when I read some of the comments posted during voting.  One here is regretable and unforgivable and you certainly know which one that is.  I have been in this community for three months and there were a few times when I could have thrown in the towel after the cavalier, almost abusive tones of some comments.  Fortunately I have a relatively thick skin (comes from 65 years of taking life''s lumps.)  I persevered through my early attempts which were rated as low 4''s, even a 3+.  I have learned from the criticisms of mature, well-meaning members, and now have a few 6+''s under my belt.  I love the idea you went after in this challenge and I would hope that you would browse the forums so that you can match up the comments with the people who made them.  This would allow you to "consider the source."Basically, I hope you don''t get discouraged.  You obviously have a great sense of humor and creativity.  Go for it!Larry', '2005-09-07 12:42:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682695, 224934, 32754, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments, I tried to give it an old time feel and some of you saw that, so that makes me happy...sorry about the trees for the tree complainers but it''s better to go parking in the woods.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments, I tried to give it an old time feel and some of you saw that, so that makes me happy...sorry about the trees for the tree complainers but it''s better to go parking in the woods.', '2005-09-07 13:06:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682703, 223695, 29906, '<td valign="top">Thanks all for your votes and comments, the final score as expected was appropriate for this shot, it''s amazing how much one could learn by submitting to these contests and comparing to the winning shots.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-09-07 12:10:19.</i></td>', 'Thanks all for your votes and comments, the final score as expected was appropriate for this shot, it''s amazing how much one could learn by submitting to these contests and comparing to the winning shots.', '2005-09-07 13:09:20.000000', '2005-09-07 13:10:19.000000', 0),
(1682711, 224301, 39440, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for the good comments. I took this shot on a street in Adams Morgan without even knowing about the contest, I was just out playing around and happened on a store display and liked the shoe. That''s why the wire basket is there. I should have taken more time to get the shoe better centered and more full-frame, I didn''t do any cropping on the shot.</td>', 'Thanks everyone for the good comments. I took this shot on a street in Adams Morgan without even knowing about the contest, I was just out playing around and happened on a store display and liked the shoe. That''s why the wire basket is there. I should have taken more time to get the shoe better centered and more full-frame, I didn''t do any cropping on the shot.', '2005-09-07 13:11:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682721, 224008, 37923, '<td valign="top">hahahaha! I really like this picture! Nice job, congrats!</td>', 'hahahaha! I really like this picture! Nice job, congrats!', '2005-09-07 13:14:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682741, 224985, 32147, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for the comments.  This was shot on a 6 day cruise in the Baltic Sea with stops in Copenhagen, Visby, Tallinn Estonia, St. Petersburg Russia, Helsinki, and return to Stockholm.  I was hired by the cruise line to shoot photos of the ship and do a virtual tour of it as well.  What a blast!  I think the photo coveys the feeling of relaxation clearly.<br/> <br/>I was really disappointed with the results of the challenge and I find myself somewhat disillusioned.  The shoe shot that I took had a delicate feel to it, it''s side lit by sunlight from the left and it made the ocean a brilliant blue.  The composition, in my mind, is well balanced in that while the black shoes occupy and weigh the lower left, the upper right is open and light.  I felt that cropping the image would result in a composition that feels more "boxed in" and cramped and it took away from the open, light feeling that I was trying to project here.<br/> <br/>At any rate, I really liked this shot.  It seems however, that the majority of voters did not.  Better luck next time, I suppose.</td>', 'Thank you all for the comments.  This was shot on a 6 day cruise in the Baltic Sea with stops in Copenhagen, Visby, Tallinn Estonia, St. Petersburg Russia, Helsinki, and return to Stockholm.  I was hired by the cruise line to shoot photos of the ship and do a virtual tour of it as well.  What a blast!  I think the photo coveys the feeling of relaxation clearly. I was really disappointed with the results of the challenge and I find myself somewhat disillusioned.  The shoe shot that I took had a delicate feel to it, it''s side lit by sunlight from the left and it made the ocean a brilliant blue.  The composition, in my mind, is well balanced in that while the black shoes occupy and weigh the lower left, the upper right is open and light.  I felt that cropping the image would result in a composition that feels more "boxed in" and cramped and it took away from the open, light feeling that I was trying to project here. At any rate, I really liked this shot.  It seems however, that the majority of voters did not.  Better luck next time, I suppose.', '2005-09-07 13:18:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682818, 223323, 117, '<td valign="top">I think you should have gotten first place as far as I''m concerned. Nice photograph be proud of this one.</td>', 'I think you should have gotten first place as far as I''m concerned. Nice photograph be proud of this one.', '2005-09-07 13:43:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682841, 222938, 22937, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your overwhelmingly nice and helpful comments folks! My first submission... and ended up at fifth place, well I''m honored (beginners luck probably). I''m currently in Scotland but will be back to ansver any Q:s in a couple of days. <br/> <br/>/Ekenborg</td>', 'Thanks for your overwhelmingly nice and helpful comments folks! My first submission... and ended up at fifth place, well I''m honored (beginners luck probably). I''m currently in Scotland but will be back to ansver any Q:s in a couple of days.  /Ekenborg', '2005-09-07 13:52:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682877, 225066, 39349, '<td valign="top">I would have expected this shot to do better than it did. I was surprised that more people didn''t think like we did. I really liked your photo, gave it a 9 during voting, good luck on the upcoming challenges!<br/> <br/></td>', 'I would have expected this shot to do better than it did. I was surprised that more people didn''t think like we did. I really liked your photo, gave it a 9 during voting, good luck on the upcoming challenges! ', '2005-09-07 13:59:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682936, 222596, 36001, '<td valign="top">Well my first effort was a complete disaster but the good thing is, I can only get better!!<br/>To be honest I''d been watching the site for ages and finally decided to take the plunge and give it a whirl. I wasn''t totally happy with my picture but decided to enter it for experience purposes.<br/>The picture was actually my wedding shoe with the hymn we sang and my wedding rings. Unfortunately it didn''t work but I did appreciate all the comments even tho'' they were all negative bar 1.<br/>I''m a glutton for punishment so I''ll be back :-)</td>', 'Well my first effort was a complete disaster but the good thing is, I can only get better!!To be honest I''d been watching the site for ages and finally decided to take the plunge and give it a whirl. I wasn''t totally happy with my picture but decided to enter it for experience purposes.The picture was actually my wedding shoe with the hymn we sang and my wedding rings. Unfortunately it didn''t work but I did appreciate all the comments even tho'' they were all negative bar 1.I''m a glutton for punishment so I''ll be back :-)', '2005-09-07 14:11:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(1682941, 222938, 26464, '<td valign="top">what a great shot. it seems to leap out of the screen. wow!<br/></td>', 'what a great shot. it seems to leap out of the screen. wow!', '2005-09-07 14:12:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(1683024, 223360, 37961, '<td valign="top">Yours has a more gold color on my monitor. Strange how you made a L lense...hehee<br/> <br/>Here was my entry. <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=222966" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/373/thumb/222966.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/373/thumb/222966.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/373/thumb/222966.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Yours has a more gold color on my monitor. Strange how you made a L lense...hehee Here was my entry. ', '2005-09-07 14:32:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1683029, 224008, 5112, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, Cole!  Beautiful image.</td>', 'Congratulations, Cole!  Beautiful image.', '2005-09-07 14:34:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1683057, 224419, 25754, '<td valign="top">Great shoes and awesome action! I''m partial to cycling images :)</td>', 'Great shoes and awesome action! I''m partial to cycling images :)', '2005-09-07 14:49:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1683265, 224815, 20887, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments!  I just wanted to take a picture of the sand and the water, not with the challenge in mind, and just thought I''d throw it out there to see what comments I would get.  It''s actually my first entry, and I would love some advice on how to do all the stuff people mentioned.  I just cropped the photo and made it smaller to fit the max file size requirement.  For future reference on photo size, how do I maximize the size?  Also, how can I avoid looking too cropped when trying to eliminate distracting elements from the photo?  Any insights would be helpful to this complete beginner.  Thanks again!</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments!  I just wanted to take a picture of the sand and the water, not with the challenge in mind, and just thought I''d throw it out there to see what comments I would get.  It''s actually my first entry, and I would love some advice on how to do all the stuff people mentioned.  I just cropped the photo and made it smaller to fit the max file size requirement.  For future reference on photo size, how do I maximize the size?  Also, how can I avoid looking too cropped when trying to eliminate distracting elements from the photo?  Any insights would be helpful to this complete beginner.  Thanks again!', '2005-09-07 15:52:12.000000', NULL, 0),
