(1686416, 225041, 42849, '<td valign="top">I;m a newbie here so maybe it''s "just me", but I think you deserved much better.   Your image seems well conceived and lit.  The understated shadowplay seem nothing short of wonderful.   I''d love to hear more about how you thought about this image...</td>', 'I;m a newbie here so maybe it''s "just me", but I think you deserved much better.   Your image seems well conceived and lit.  The understated shadowplay seem nothing short of wonderful.   I''d love to hear more about how you thought about this image...', '2005-09-08 11:07:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1686435, 225000, 31115, '<td valign="top">Thank you to all those that commented. Just to answer a couple remarks. <br/> <br/>I wanted the summer-like feel to it, B&amp;W or Sepia doesn''t cut it. <br/> <br/>I did try an image taken from the front, it didn''t work for me. <br/> <br/>And lastly, the crop of this photo is the only one that would work. If I cropped the half a foot on either side, I can only imagine how odd that would that look. Think about it. And if I cropped any wider, it would become a panoramic.<br/> <br/>Nope, this is the photo I wanted. I got a 5.8, oh well. I am still happy with it.<br/> <br/>JM<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-09-08 10:18:19.</i></td>', 'Thank you to all those that commented. Just to answer a couple remarks.  I wanted the summer-like feel to it, B&W or Sepia doesn''t cut it.  I did try an image taken from the front, it didn''t work for me.  And lastly, the crop of this photo is the only one that would work. If I cropped the half a foot on either side, I can only imagine how odd that would that look. Think about it. And if I cropped any wider, it would become a panoramic. Nope, this is the photo I wanted. I got a 5.8, oh well. I am still happy with it. JM', '2005-09-08 11:16:14.000000', '2005-09-08 11:18:19.000000', 0),
